## Keep Lakebase quality SQL on the Build warehouse
================================================================================

Context: Deployed data-quality checks on a Lakebase domain failed with
"Could not read the knowledge graph — is it built?" wrapping
`use_kernel=True does not support a custom credentials_provider`. Quality
SQL always used `engine="view"`, which followed the Lakehouse//RT query
warehouse even when the domain graph lives in Lakebase. Thrift then
rejected RT and the Apps OAuth retry kept `credentials_provider` next to
`use_kernel`.

Changes:

1. src/back/core/graphdb/GraphDBFactory.py
   Bind `engine="view"` to the Build SQL Warehouse with `use_sea=False`.
2. src/back/core/databricks/SQLWarehouse.py
   On a Thrift-to-Kernel retry, drop `credentials_provider` and pass
   Apps M2M `oauth_client_id` / `oauth_client_secret`.
3. tests/units/dtwin/test_triplestore_factory.py
   Assert view-store clients ignore the RT query warehouse.
4. tests/units/core/test_sql_warehouse.py
   Assert the Apps Kernel retry does not keep `credentials_provider`.
5. docs/backend.md
   Document that `engine="view"` uses the Build warehouse.
6. docs/architecture.md
   Note that quality SQL never follows the RT query warehouse.

